{"id": "5730b10b8ab72b1400f9c69f", "group_id": "United_Methodist_Church", "input": "Article: United_Methodist_Church\nPassage: The United Methodist Church upholds the sanctity of human life both of the child and the mother. As a result, the church is \"reluctant to affirm abortion as an acceptable practice,\" and condemns the use of late-term or partial birth abortion except as a medical necessity. The denomination as a whole is committed to \"assist[ing] the ministry of crisis pregnancy centers and pregnancy resource centers that compassionately help women find feasible alternatives to abortion.\" Still, the denomination is pro-choice and also \"was a founding member of the Religious Coalition for Reproductive Choice...[and] 2008 General Conference [went] on record in support of the work of the Religious Coalition for Reproductive Choice\".\nQuestion: When did the General Conference go on record in support of the work of the Religious Coalition for Reproductive Choice?"}
