{"id": "570d9c7616d0071400510beb", "group_id": "Adolescence", "input": "Article: Adolescence\nPassage: There are at least two major approaches to understanding cognitive change during adolescence. One is the constructivist view of cognitive development. Based on the work of Piaget, it takes a quantitative, state-theory approach, hypothesizing that adolescents' cognitive improvement is relatively sudden and drastic. The second is the information-processing perspective, which derives from the study of artificial intelligence and attempts to explain cognitive development in terms of the growth of specific components of the thinking process.\nQuestion: What view towards cognitive development during adolescence did Piaget take?"}
